{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "600152de-17a2-49fc-adad-ad1be77f6646",
    "name": "ProcureX",
    "description": "# API Collection Documentation\n\n## Overview\n\nThis Postman collection contains the REST APIs developed for the **ProcureX** procurement management platform. It serves as a centralized workspace for testing, validating, and documenting backend services during development.\n\nThe collection is organized into logical modules based on business functionality, enabling developers and testers to efficiently interact with different microservices through a unified interface. Each request includes the necessary HTTP methods, headers, request bodies, authentication requirements, and expected responses wherever applicable.\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe primary objectives of this Postman collection are to:\n\n- Simplify API development and testing.\n    \n- Validate request and response workflows.\n    \n- Verify authentication and authorization mechanisms.\n    \n- Test business logic and data validation.\n    \n- Support integration between frontend and backend services.\n    \n- Provide reusable examples for developers and QA teams.\n    \n\n## Usage\n\n1. Import the Postman collection into Postman.\n    \n2. Configure the required environment variables.\n    \n3. Start the necessary backend services.\n    \n4. Authenticate before accessing protected resources.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "56854052",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/56854052-600152de-17a2-49fc-adad-ad1be77f6646?source=collection_link"
  },
